Subject: theme: hold the caller's default theme from the start

What: ThemeProvider's `defaultTheme` is a parsed DesktopTheme rather than an id, held in the store beside oc-2; theme/codex-theme.ts exports the parsed Codex theme.
Why: a default theme named by id loaded through the themes glob as its own chunk during boot (codex-*.js, one static round trip, 116 ms on a 100 ms link) and applied only after it arrived; held, it applies in the first render and no theme chunk loads unless the reader picked another theme.

